course: dictionary
lesson: 3773
title: One word, many feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word fond can mean several things, and the words around it tell you which meaning fits. «He is new and pink and fat and small, and the Woman is very fond of him.» Here fond of means she likes him a lot and cares about him.
explain: Fond can also describe a look, a smile or a memory that is warm and loving. «A fond smile» shows love, and «fond memories» are happy memories that bring a warm feeling back. Use the clues around the word, just as you did with famished and curt.
explain: Fond of can also mean liking to do something often. «He's fond of telling jokes» means he tells jokes a lot because he enjoys it. Be careful: a fond hope is a foolish hope that is unlikely to come true, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Fond means liking someone or something a lot, as in «I'm fond of my grandma».
fact: Fond also means loving and warm, as in «a fond smile» and «fond memories».
fact: Fond of doing something means you like to do it often, as in «he's fond of telling jokes».
fact: A fond hope or belief is a foolish one that is unlikely to come true.
fact: In Scotland, «wee man» is a fond way to say little lad.
exercise: «He is new and pink and fat and small, and the Woman is very fond of him.» What does fond of mean here? | Bored of | Afraid of | Angry with | *Likes a lot
exercise: Which phrase shows a warm, loving feeling? | *a fond smile | a long queue | a sudden shout | a cold stare
exercise: Mia says, «I'm fond of doing puzzles.» What does she mean? | She is good at puzzles only once | *She likes doing puzzles and does them often | She hates puzzles | She was forced to do puzzles
test: What does a fond hope mean? | A hope written in a letter | A small hope said loudly | *A foolish hope that is unlikely to come true | A hope that is certain to happen
test: In a letter, «fondest wishes» shows what kind of feeling? | *Warm love and care | Anger | Surprise | Boredom
exam: «Grandad is fond of his old armchair, and he sits in it every evening.» What does fond of show? | He has never seen it | He wants to sell it | He is afraid of it | *He likes it a lot
